{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]The line of David [Eb]stands
Through Hanani[Bb]ah and Repha[Eb]iah
Obadi[Gm7]ah and Shecani[Eb]ah
[Cm7]Names recorded in the [Fsus4]book
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Hattush I[F/A]gal Ba[Gm]riah
Nea[Eb]riah and [Bb/D]Shaphat [F]too
[Gm]Six [Dm7]sons of She[Eb]maiah
[Cm7]Counted in the [F]ancient [Bb]scroll [Eb][Bb][Eb]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]After the exile [Eb]deep
The royal [Bb]line was kept a[Eb]live
She[Gm]maiah had six [Eb]sons
Their [Cm7]names were written [Fsus4]down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Hattush I[F/A]gal Ba[Gm]riah
Nea[Eb]riah and [Bb/D]Shaphat [F]too
[Gm]Six sons [Dm7]of She[Eb]maiah
[Cm7]Counted in the [F]ancient [Bb]scroll
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
From Shecaniah [Eb]to She[Gm]maiah
The [Bb]bloodline holds its [F]ground
Preser[Eb]ved through the [F]years of wait[Gm]ing
In the [Cm7]land and far a[Fsus4][F]way
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
